---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Win from '../components/Win.astro';
---

<Base title="Colophon" description="How v0id.me is built: Astro on Cloudflare Workers, no JavaScript for readers, and a status signed on my Mac.">
  <Win title="Read Me: Colophon" as="main" class="w-md">
    <h1 class="visually-hidden">Colophon</h1>
    <div class="win-body readme">
      <p class="label">the site</p>
      <p>Astro on Cloudflare Workers. Every page is plain HTML and CSS; no JavaScript is sent to readers. The desktop, the windows, the static and the 88x31 buttons are all CSS.</p>
      <p>Posts are markdown files, edited directly or through Sveltia CMS. The source is <a href="https://github.com/v0id-user/peace-land">on GitHub</a>.</p>

      <p class="label">now spinning and fahad's mac</p>
      <p>The Worker asks Spotify for what is playing when the home page loads, and says whether it is playing, paused or quiet.</p>
      <p>The status comes from a reporter on my Mac. It reads the lid, whether I am at the keyboard, and my Claude Code sessions, and sends only what changed. Before the Mac sleeps it says so.</p>
      <p>Every report is signed with <a href="/pgp/">my OpenPGP key</a>. The Worker holds only the public key and drops anything it cannot verify, and anyone can check the last report with <code>curl -sL v0id.me/status.asc | gpg -d</code>.</p>
      <p>The git row shows my newest commit in a public repo. Private repos are filtered out before any commit is looked at. The tab icon fades to gray when I am away and pale when the laptop sleeps.</p>

      <p class="label">from a terminal</p>
      <p><code>curl -L v0id.me</code> answers in plain text, my key is found with <code>gpg --locate-keys hey@v0id.me</code>, and the <a href="/guestbook/">guestbook</a> can be signed with curl. The full list is under <a href="/misc/">misc</a>.</p>
      <p>Guestbook entries wait for me to approve them with a command signed by the same key.</p>
    </div>
  </Win>
</Base>
